====Trainer Tower====
Trainer Tower sets a goal for challengers of battling through eight floors of opponents to reach the rooftop as quickly as possible. There are four different types of battle in which challengers may participate: {{DL|Trainer Tower|Single Mode}}, {{DL|Trainer Tower|Double Mode}}, {{DL|Trainer Tower|Knockout Mode}}, and {{DL|Trainer Tower|Mixed Mode}}. The first time the player beats each mode earns them a rare item, which can only be obtained once. Unlike most battle facilities, a challenger's Pokémon are not healed between battles, though recovery items like [[Revive]]s and [[Potion]]s may be used. If necessary, challengers can return to the entrance to heal their party at the Pokémon Center, though this will waste more time in comparison to using items. Battles do not award [[experience]] or money, and the levels of the opposing Trainers' Pokémon match that of the player's highest-leveled party Pokémon.

